%---------------- ISPF Tutorial 2 of 5: Dynamic Areas --------------------%
%Command ===>_ZCMD
+
 ULS uses an AREA(DYNAMIC) field. The exec builds fixed-width records
 containing a data set name, volume, migration flag, and device.
+
 The panel binds that field to DYNAREA and DYNSHAD. Each row starts
 with a DATAIN attribute for the one-character action field, followed
 by DATAOUT for the row text. DYNSHAD supplies optional display styling.
 B, E, and V open the selected data set. I opens a scrollable details
 panel with its organization, DCB, space allocation, and status.
+
 The exec rebuilds the visible slice before DISPLAY. Scroll verbs and
 the UP/DOWN commands move the first row; the dynamic area then shows
 the new slice.
+
 Enter NEXT, PREV, 1-5, or END to navigate.
)END
